// # os — Operating System Surface
//
// Logline: The OS syscall shims (sys_exec, sys_args, sys_prctl), the policy getenv filter (OODA_/OO_ keys only), the file I/O surface, the net-floor loopback constraint, the host process info, the rlimit setter, the time+rand source, the DNS resolver (loopback-only), and the Landlock-gated proc_mem.
//
// Setup: All operations are cap-gated. Process control and FS require their respective caps. DNS resolution is loopback-only by design (no getaddrinfo).
//
// Beats:
//   1. Read sys.c — sys_exec, sys_args, policy getenv, child filter env.
//   2. Read fs.c — file I/O with cap-gated path safety.
//   3. Read netfloor.c — net-floor loopback constraint.
//   4. Read host.c — host process info (pid, ppid, etc.).
//   5. Read dns.h — the OoDNS resolver type and loopback constraint.
//   6. Read dns.c — the resolver; only loopback allowed.
//   7. Read rlimit.c — setrlimit wrapper (RLIMIT_AS, RLIMIT_NOFILE, RLIMIT_CPU).
//   8. Read time_rand.c — monotonic time + secure random.
//
// ──▓▓ os ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: fail-closed: no getaddrinfo, no unrestricted env ::
